// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/best-treadmills-with-brushless-motor/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "best");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-24",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-24",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "brushless treadmill",
      "treadmill with brushless motor",
      "best brushless treadmill",
      "brushless walking pad",
      "brushless motor treadmill",
      "quiet brushless treadmill",
      "is a brushless treadmill better",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best Overall: Sunny Health & Fitness Auto Incline Treadmill", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/best/">Best Treadmills</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buying Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">Best Treadmills With Brushless Motors What the Label Buys, and the Picks Worth It</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        The best treadmill with a brushless motor for most homes is Sunny Health & Fitness’s fully assembled Auto Incline treadmill: a 2.5 HP brushless motor, 10 mph, 15% incline and a 20 by 53-inch deck for about $598 on Amazon. Brushless means no carbon brushes to wear out and a little less motor noise; it does not mean more power, and six other picks cover running, premium, budget and walking pads.
      </p>
      <p class="ed-answer"><strong>Short answer.</strong> Best Overall: <a href="#sunny-auto-incline-brushless">Sunny Health & Fitness Auto Incline Treadmill</a>. Best Under $500: <a href="#sunny-smart-wifi-brushless">Sunny Health & Fitness Smart Wi-Fi Treadmill</a>. Best for Running: <a href="#urevo-cybermega">UREVO CyberMega</a>.</p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 24, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS<br />
          <span class="ed-method">How we chose: makers’ published specifications and manuals, independent reviews and owner reports, cross-checked. Not tested hands-on.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We may earn a commission when you buy through the links below. It costs you nothing and never decides a ranking. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <figure class="ed-hero">
        <div class="ed-hero-collage">
          <a href="#sunny-auto-incline-brushless"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/4132OQswF8L._SL500_.jpg" alt="Sunny Health &amp; Fitness Auto Incline Treadmill" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#urevo-cybermega"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ENKZ3LzYL._SL500_.jpg" alt="UREVO CyberMega" width="500" height="500" decoding="async" /></a>
          <a href="#sole-f85"><img src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/313FL2pZ45L._SL500_.jpg" alt="Sole F85" width="500" height="333" decoding="async" /></a>
        </div>
        <figcaption>Sunny Health &amp; Fitness Auto Incline Treadmill · UREVO CyberMega · Sole F85</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          “Brushless” has gone from a line in a spec sheet to a headline word on Amazon. Walking pads at
          $150 and folding treadmills at $300 now put it in their titles next to the horsepower, usually
          with “quiet” beside it. It is a real engineering difference: a brushless motor has no carbon
          brushes rubbing on a commutator, so it loses a wear part and a source of noise. But it is a
          description of how the motor is built, not a measure of how strong it is, and a weak brushless
          motor is still a weak motor. This page explains what the label actually buys, then picks seven
